VISUAL CHECK
  Headless browser already present. 2 captures of index.html, 3 corrective edits, 1 recapture.
  Capture 1 found real breakage: everything below the telemetry strip rendered blank. The
  scroll-reveal hid all content at opacity 0 and only restored it when an IntersectionObserver
  entry fired, so any environment that does not scroll (and any visitor without JS) got an
  empty page below the hero.
  Fixes, all in index.html:
    1. .reveal is visible by default; the hidden state is scoped under html.js.
    2. An inline head script sets that js class, so the hidden state only ever exists when
       JS is running to undo it.
    3. A 2500ms safety net reveals anything the observer has not already reached and fills
       its charge columns.
  Recapture confirms the full page: features, testimonials with headshots, pricing ladder,
  closing band and footer all present, no overlap, no off-canvas elements, headshots at 1:1.
  demo.html was not captured (capture budget spent on the landing page).
